1
00:32:12,055 --> 00:32:13,222
Mangal Singhku: In our Ho society

2
00:32:14,349 --> 00:32:16,559
there is a tradition of Guan Bunga (cattle pen worship).

3
00:32:16,851 --> 00:32:19,312
And the Guan Bunga is,

4
00:32:19,312 --> 00:32:21,939
in a Ho house,

5
00:32:22,148 --> 00:32:22,857
Guan means...

6
00:32:22,857 --> 00:32:24,484
a pen where cattle live

7
00:32:25,109 --> 00:32:26,235
..where [cattle] are tied...

8
00:32:26,235 --> 00:32:28,154
this is called Guan.

9
00:32:28,571 --> 00:32:30,907
The worship in a pen is called Guan Bunga.

10
00:32:31,407 --> 00:32:33,576
This is how Guan Bunga is done...

11
00:32:34,077 --> 00:32:35,161
The family head,

12
00:32:36,621 --> 00:32:38,623
after [his] morning shower,

13
00:32:39,415 --> 00:32:40,958
[wears] a new <i>dhoti</i>,

14
00:32:41,334 --> 00:32:43,795
new clothes...wears,

15
00:32:44,587 --> 00:32:48,049
after cleaning the cattle pen,

16
00:32:48,633 --> 00:32:51,886
in the place of worship, smears cow dung

17
00:32:52,428 --> 00:32:53,471
After smearing cow dung,

18
00:32:54,263 --> 00:32:56,516
there, [gather] vermillion, rice,

19
00:32:57,350 --> 00:32:58,851
gathers and worships.

20
00:32:59,519 --> 00:33:02,980
And, with that, worships a chicken.

21
00:33:04,524 --> 00:33:07,568
And the cattle

22
00:33:09,362 --> 00:33:12,699
are removed from the pen.

23
00:33:13,157 --> 00:33:14,909
The worship rituals happen there [cattle pen].

24
00:33:15,493 --> 00:33:18,162
And, with that,

25
00:33:18,579 --> 00:33:22,750
he prays in front of the home deities.

26
00:33:23,334 --> 00:33:24,919
[he] prays saying that the cattle pen there...

27
00:33:24,919 --> 00:33:29,757
stays pure there.

28
00:33:30,007 --> 00:33:31,634
[He] prays it stays divine.

29
00:33:48,276 --> 00:33:49,235
In Guan Bunga,

30
00:33:49,569 --> 00:33:51,904
patriarch of a house worships

31
00:33:52,572 --> 00:33:54,615
because the entire year, for us...

32
00:33:55,408 --> 00:33:58,286
the cattle help us with [agricultural] work.

33
00:33:58,661 --> 00:34:00,705
We toil [them] for our occupations.

34
00:34:01,122 --> 00:34:03,958
So for their [cattle's] protection,

35
00:34:04,375 --> 00:34:10,298
the village <i>desauli</i> (chief) [prays] Guan Bunga, Burubunga...

36
00:34:10,715 --> 00:34:12,091
..prays and begs before them.

37
00:34:12,467 --> 00:34:15,011
That we toiled year-around,

38
00:34:15,470 --> 00:34:18,347
made them work hard...made them work hard.

39
00:34:18,347 --> 00:34:21,642
they [grazed near] forests, rivers, ponds.

40
00:34:22,351 --> 00:34:25,438
And everywhere they go grazing,

41
00:34:25,897 --> 00:34:27,899
may they don't fall down then!

42
00:34:28,357 --> 00:34:30,318
May the <i>bageya</i> hide [them] in the forest!

43
00:34:31,569 --> 00:34:34,197
May the tigers and the bears don't hunt [cattle]!

44
00:34:34,739 --> 00:34:36,783
Besides this,

45
00:34:36,908 --> 00:34:39,911
they give birth to calves yearlong.

46
00:34:40,787 --> 00:34:46,626
And in the village, may [people] stay well and don't fall sick!

47
00:34:47,335 --> 00:34:49,796
May the ticks not attack their bodies, and may scorpions not bite!

48
00:34:50,296 --> 00:34:53,800
So, in front of Buru Bunga,

49
00:34:54,675 --> 00:35:01,182
and Guan Bunga, and Marang Bunga, he (chief) prays.

50
00:35:01,599 --> 00:35:02,975
The deities listen to this.

51
00:35:03,434 --> 00:35:04,936
Then, year-around,

52
00:35:06,604 --> 00:35:11,317
By the grace of the deity, they [cattle] stay healthy.
